# Study Notes Style

This repository is for folders and Markdown notes about technologies that were practiced or learned.

- Treat each note as a quick memory refresher, not a long-form article.
- Prefer short sections made of short paragraphs over long bullet lists.
- Question and answer format is encouraged when it makes the note clearer.
- Use bullets only when they genuinely make scanning easier.
- Avoid stacking many tiny bullet points when one short paragraph says it better.
- Remove project-specific names, IDs, and one-off examples unless the user explicitly wants them kept.
- Avoid filler, repetition, storytelling, and walls of text.
- Optimize for fast scanning and a clear flow of understanding.
- Use diagrams when they improve comprehension, especially for flows, relationships, or architecture.
- Prefer practical structure such as: what it is, why it matters, key concepts, setup or usage, common pitfalls, and quick examples.
- Surface the most important ideas first.
- Keep wording simple and direct so the reader can refresh quickly.
